WEBVTT

L1
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.849
Every tavern in Millbrook tells the same story.

L2
00:00:09.349 --> 00:00:16.854
Brave heroes ride out. Monsters fall. Gold comes home. Everyone cheers.

L3
00:00:17.254 --> 00:00:24.299
Funny thing about that story. It never says whose door they kicked in.

L4
00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:32.453
Millbrook pays by the head. Wolf pelts. Goblin ears. Anything that lives in the dark.

L5
00:00:33.053 --> 00:00:40.921
For a hundred years, the town grew fat on what its heroes carried home. And the wilds grew quiet.

L6
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:42.339
Too quiet.

L7
00:00:44.439 --> 00:00:48.896
Until something old remembered how to be angry.

L8
00:00:49.546 --> 00:00:56.373
A lich. A dragon. A prince of the Pit. Which one doesn't matter.

L9
00:00:57.373 --> 00:01:01.468
The monsters have no heroes. They have you.

L10
00:01:02.268 --> 00:01:08.273
You start small. Two servants. One lair. A tower nobody visits.

L11
00:01:08.673 --> 00:01:13.952
Win the wilds back with gold, with lies, or with your fists.

L12
00:01:14.452 --> 00:01:19.199
Then send them down the road, to the town that sent the heroes.

L13
00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:23.506
Burn Millbrook's hall, and the bounties stop.

L14
00:01:24.606 --> 00:01:31.434
Mind you, Millbrook won't make it easy. Its heroes get stronger every day.

L15
00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:35.941
And sooner or later, they'll come up your stairs.

L16
00:01:36.941 --> 00:01:38.133
Let them.
